## Assurance Levels

| Level | Meaning | Required Artifacts |
|-------|---------|-------------------|
| ✅ Verified (N) | Kani harness passes at instance bound N | Harness in repo, registry row with bound, size-independence argument if N < deployed capacity |
| ✅ Tested | Covered by tests on host and/or hardware | Tests in repo, Decisions row explaining why not Verified |
| ✅ Trusted | Assumed without proof | TA ID, mitigation, cited from code |

### Size-Independence Argument

When a property is verified at N below the deployed capacity, the registry row links to
a short argument that the code does not branch on the value of N except through bounds
checks. Acceptable forms: the structure is a const-generic instantiation and the
operation is written once for all N; or the operation touches at most k entries
regardless of N and the bound exceeds k. Anything weaker is a Test, not a Verify.

### Default Bounds

| Structure kind | Harness N | Deployed N |
|----------------|-----------|------------|
| {{tables}} | {{4}} | {{4096}} |
| {{rings}} | {{4}} | {{256}} |
| {{packet buffers in harness}} | {{128 bytes}} | {{2048}} |

