## Harness Conventions

| Convention | Rule |
|------------|------|
| Naming | `check_<id lowercased, hyphens to underscores>`, e.g. `check_inv_nat_003`. One harness per ID minimum. |
| Location | `{{src/harness.rs or src/kani/}}` in the crate that owns the operation, gated `#[cfg(kani)]` |
| Symbolic input | `kani::any()` for state and arguments; `kani::assume(inv(&abs(&s)))` to start valid |
| Bounds | Instance size via const generic instantiation in the harness; unwind via `#[kani::unwind(n)]` matching the spec harness plan |
| Contracts | `#[kani::requires]` / `#[kani::ensures]` on the operation, referencing `model::` predicates; verified with `#[kani::proof_for_contract]` |
| Stubs | Hardware traits replaced by model devices; `#[kani::stub]` only where a trait boundary is not possible, and then recorded in the harness plan |
| Abstraction | Each pure crate exposes `fn abs(&Impl) -> model::State`; harnesses never inspect concrete state directly |
| CI | {{how harnesses run in CI, which are gated as slow}} |

