## Concurrency Model

{{Describe the ownership discipline for this project. Example:}}

- Every piece of state names exactly one owning core. Only that core reads or writes it.
- Cross-core communication is through single-producer single-consumer rings only.
- {{Core 1}} polls and takes no interrupts; its code is sequential.
- {{Core 0}} takes interrupts for {{UART}}; its interrupt handlers touch only
  {{a dedicated input ring}} and nothing the main loop touches.
- The rings are the one shared-memory structure. Their barrier placement is TA-PLAT-006.

### Rings

| Ring | Producer Core | Consumer Core | Carries | Spec |
|------|---------------|---------------|---------|------|
| {{cmd}} | {{0}} | {{1}} | {{route and rule updates}} | {{ring spec}} |
| {{exc}} | {{1}} | {{0}} | {{exception packets, stats}} | {{ring spec}} |

